   <dc:title>Towards the solution of an integrable spin chain</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Nepomechie, Rafael I.</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Pimenta, Rodrigo A.</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>Retore, Ana L. [UNESP]</dc:creator>
   <dc:contributor>University of Miami</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>Université d&amp;apos;Orléans</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>Ministry of Education of Brazil</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>Universidade de São Paulo (USP)</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>Universidade Estadual Paulista (Unesp)</dc:contributor>
   <dc:subject>Bethe ansatz</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>integrable quantum spin chains</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>quantum group</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Two branches of integrable open quantum-group invariant Dn+1 (2) quantum spin chains are known. For one branch (ϵ = 0), a complete Bethe ansatz solution has been proposed. However, the other branch (ϵ = 1) has so far resisted solution. In an effort to address this problem, we consider here the simplest case n = 1. We propose a Bethe ansatz solution, which however is not complete, as it describes only the transfer-matrix eigenvalues with odd degeneracy. We also consider a proposal for the missing eigenvalues.</dc:description>
